# Review ownership.
#
# Requires "Require review from Code Owners" in branch protection to take
# effect. Without it, these entries only auto-request reviewers.
#
# Last match wins, so the most specific rules go last.
#
# CODEOWNERS silently ignores an entry naming a user without write access on
# this repo. Verify via the CODEOWNERS errors view after any change here.

# Default: any change needs a maintainer.
*                       @sfc-gh-chorgan @sfc-gh-lhartzell

/skills/                @sfc-gh-chorgan @sfc-gh-lhartzell
/plugins/               @sfc-gh-chorgan @sfc-gh-lhartzell

# Process docs. Changing the review bar should be reviewed by the people who
# hold that bar.
/CONTRIBUTING.md        @sfc-gh-chorgan @sfc-gh-lhartzell
/MAINTAINING.md         @sfc-gh-chorgan @sfc-gh-lhartzell
/README.md              @sfc-gh-chorgan @sfc-gh-lhartzell

# Automation runs with repository credentials.
/.github/               @sfc-gh-chorgan @sfc-gh-lhartzell

# Executable code shipped inside a skill.
#
# CODEOWNERS has no reliable recursive glob, so this matches one level only.
# The escalation labeler covers nested script paths by content instead.
/skills/*/scripts/      @sfc-gh-chorgan @sfc-gh-lhartzell
